t2_waived: "No use case moves and no decision is made. All three costs are cost, not behaviour - the rendered output is identical everywhere the existing suite can see it, which is the proof the WU was asked to produce (741 pre-existing assertions pass unchanged). DEC-22's four forks - absolute, seconds, local, 24h - are preserved exactly and re-asserted by three added boundary tests rather than merely left alone. The one design record this WU does move lives in the code, where DEC-16 puts it: TextRenderer's TSDoc gains a @props line stating that `size` is the body's own byte count and that a caller may pass it only where the text is a whole decode of those bytes. That is a T4 fact and is accounted for on the cr/v3 note's design.undesigned entry for the file, not here - doc/v1 models docs/ only. FormRenderer's TSDoc is unchanged because its component is, and DEC-16 expressly refuses rejected-alternative rationale in a TSDoc. The one T2-shaped candidate this WU raises, the discipline that a performance fix lands only against a number, is the epic's own stated rule and belongs in its distillation at W10; writing it into a WU report would be duplicating downward. One T1 gap is recorded as a follow-up rather than taken: testing-strategy.html's tooling table does not mention the benchmark, and that edit needs a listed authoriser."
